# LF everywhere, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Not a style preference: ops/aircast-signal.service and the coturn and nginx
# templates are read by Linux daemons, and a CRLF sneaking into a systemd unit
# or a shell snippet fails in ways that read as a config bug. Checking out LF
# on Windows too keeps what is edited identical to what is deployed.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Things git must never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.mkv binary
*.jar binary
*.keystore binary
*.aar binary
gradlew.bat text eol=crlf
